+# Stock research
+
+## Request paths and model
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java` exposes both checkout endpoints and delegates to `OrderFacade.processOrder`. The authenticated endpoint catches every exception and converts it to `503`, so an inventory conflict cannot currently become `409`.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartApi.java` exposes cart creation, single modification, and `/multi`; non-resource exceptions are wrapped in `ServiceRuntimeException`, whose handler returns `400`.
+- `sm-core-model/.../catalog/product/availability/ProductAvailability.java` stores stock in `productQuantity`. This is the quantity surfaced by the v2 product response.
+- `sm-core-model/.../order/orderproduct/OrderProduct.java` stores the durable order line's `sku` and `productQuantity`; its `id` is the order-line primary key, not a product id.
+
+## Causes found
+
+1. `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java` calls `productService.getById(orderProduct.getId())`. This confuses the order-line id with the product id, so it can decrement another product or find none. It loops all availabilities and decrements without selecting the ordered product by SKU. If stock is insufficient it only logs an error and continues with a negative quantity. It also calls `paymentService.processPayment` and persists the order before inventory validation/decrement, so a failed stock check cannot be atomic.
+2. `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.createCartItem` and `createCartItems` reject null/zero availability but do not reject a requested quantity above stock. The multi-item check is written as `quantity > 0 && quantity == null || quantity == 0`, so operator precedence makes the null/zero branch unsafe and still does not compare requested quantity to stock. Existing-item increments in `addItemsToShoppingCart` also happen after item creation and are not checked against the combined quantity. `updateCartItem` and `updateCartItems` assign requested quantities without stock validation; the multi update mutates managed line items while validating, so a later failure can leave partial changes.
+3. `OrderFacadeImpl.updateOrderStatus` returns for duplicate statuses but otherwise just changes status/history. It neither restores stock on the first transition to `CANCELED` nor rejects transitions away from an already canceled order. There is no cancellation marker beyond order status, so the status transition itself must be the idempotency boundary.
+4. `ReadableProductPopulator` sets quantity from an availability and only sets `canBePurchased=true` when quantity is positive and the product is marked available. It does not explicitly set `available=false` for zero stock, and its quantity loop can leave output dependent on arbitrary availability-set iteration. The required response semantics need stock positivity combined with merchant availability.
+
+## Other affected behavior
+
+- `OrderServiceImpl.process` is the common checkout path for both APIs, so inventory validation/decrement belongs there and must be transactional before order/payment side effects where possible.
+- Product availability is represented by a set and can contain variants/regions. Existing checkout/cart code treats all availabilities as stock, while v2 chooses one arbitrary availability. The implementation should use the product's default/current availability consistently with the existing API behavior and SKU lookup.
+- `RestErrorHandler` maps `ServiceRuntimeException` to `400`; a dedicated conflict exception/handler or explicit `409` response is required for stock/cart/status conflicts.
+- Existing integration tests are in `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/cart/ShoppingCartAPIIntegrationTest.java`; order/catalog tests and module Maven poms should be used to add/execute focused coverage.
+
+## Intended correction
+
+Centralize stock lookup/validation by product SKU, validate the whole cart before any checkout side effects, decrement only the matching availability by each line quantity, and make the service transaction roll back on conflict. Validate prospective cart state before saving (including combined additions and all multi changes). On the first cancellation, restore each line's matching product stock; reject any later non-canceled status. Make the v2 flags explicitly reflect both merchant availability and positive stock.
